cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this package, please cite it, and cite the sources of the text its questions quote (listed under references and in CREDITS.md)."
title: "sdg-tech-impact-tagger: labelling texts with SDGs, digital technologies and their impact through LLMs, by versioned questions"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/KnuxV/sdg-tech-impact-tagger"
url: "https://github.com/KnuxV/sdg-tech-impact-tagger"
abstract: >-
  A Python package that labels texts with an LLM behind any OpenAI-compatible
  endpoint: the UN Sustainable Development Goals, advanced digital
  technologies, the impact of a technology on a goal, or any list of labels
  a user writes. Questions are versioned prompt blocks identified by a hash
  and read by one of four readouts; they are chained by unit rules in a
  declarative TOML workflow. Every call is cached with its raw answer, every
  row records the model the endpoint reports, and a run can be replayed from
  its cache without the network. The package ships the questions and
  workflows of earlier research runs and rebuilds their tables row for row
  from their caches.
keywords:
  - sustainable development goals
  - SDG
  - digital technologies
  - LLM
  - annotation
  - text labelling
  - reproducibility
  - bibliometrics
